{"type":"text","timestamp":1792551875637,"sessionID":"ses_ea39876d7ffe6f5aZMqB3WhOtI","part":{"id":"prt_15c6ae0db001DUnhIpHhm7qAco","messageID":"msg_15c6a718c001df4oPAr94cph0T","sessionID":"ses_ea39876d7ffe6f5aZMqB3WhOtI","type":"text","text":"{\"items\":[{\"ref\":\"p1:step\",\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"page_quote\":\"We identify alkaline phosphatase (ALPL) as the primary receptor used by VCAP-102 to cross the BBB and demonstrate that direct binding of VCAP-102 to human ALPL can initiate receptor-mediated transcytosis in a cell barrier model.\",\"note\":\"The quote confirms receptor identification and transcytosis initiation; the paper also describes the Retrogenix/ORFeome screens, SPR, and MDCK Transwell assay, matching the step as described.\"},{\"ref\":\"p1:activity\",\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"page_quote\":\"At AAIC 2026, Voyager presented 6-month good laboratory practice (GLP) toxicology non-human primate (NHP) data showing VY1706 was well tolerated and resulted in sustained tau protein reduction by up to 75% in key AD brain regions following a single intravenous (IV) dose.\",\"note\":\"Page confirms VY1706 as a TRACER-derived capsid gene therapy, the AAIC 2026 GLP NHP data, Q4 2026 dosing in early AD, and lists ALPL-VYGR-NeuroShuttle under the wholly-owned pipeline.\"},{\"ref\":\"p1:c1\",\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"page_quote\":\"After the initial library cloning and virus production, the naive library contained approximately 4E7 individual capsid variants as identified by next generation sequencing (NGS) (Figure 1 A, step 1).\",\"note\":\"The same page states library diversity fell after the first macaque passage and that after a second in vivo selection 1,500 variants of interest were identified.\"},{\"ref\":\"p1:c2\",\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"page_quote\":\"For this, we undertook two orthogonal approaches, a capsid binding screen using the Retrogenix cell microarray of human surface proteins and a transduction screen using cells stably transduced with a lentiviral human ORFeome library (Figures S6 A and S6B).\",\"note\":\"Directly matches the two orthogonal experimental screens.\"},{\"ref\":\"p1:c3\",\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"page_quote\":\"Ectopic expression of human ALPL induced a dramatic >100-fold increase in the transcytosis of VCAP-102 while it had no measurable impact on AAV9 migration (Figure 4 F).\",\"note\":\"Quote and page context confirm the MDCK Transwell polarized-barrier result.\"},{\"ref\":\"p1:c4\",\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"page_quote\":\"100% conservation of predicted capsid-ALPL interacting residues\",\"note\":\"The deck pairs this with ~98% ALPL sequence homology (cyno/human) as the cross-species translatability argument.\"},{\"ref\":\"p1:done\",\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"page_quote\":\"We show that ectopic expression of ALPL in a polarized cell layer is sufficient to mediate transcytosis of VCAP-102 and provide in vivo evidence that capsid-receptor interaction is directly correlated with brain transduction.\",\"note\":\"Page also reports SPR affinity (~20 nM), cryo-EM density at the VR-IV/threefold apex, and AlphaFold-Multimer-derived contact residues; no exhaustive pose-depth sweep is presented.\"},{\"ref\":\"p2:step\",\"status\":\"PARTIAL\",\"page_quote\":\"Automated Pair-wise Peptide-Receptor binding model AnalysIs for Screening Engineered proteins (APPRAISE) is a method that predicts the receptor binding propensity of engineered proteins based on high-precision protein structure prediction tools, such as AlphaFold2-multimer.\",\"note\":\"README supports pairwise AF-Multimer receptor-binding prediction, but not the atom-counting/angle/pocket-depth scoring details, ten models per competition, or single-GPU Colab scale; those come from the linked paper rather than this page.\"},{\"ref\":\"p2:activity\",\"status\":\"PARTIAL\",\"page_quote\":\"Current APPRAISE supports backend-specific input generation for legacy ColabFold/AlphaFold-style FASTA files as well as newer open-source multimer tools including Boltz-1, Chai-1, and OpenFold3.\",\"note\":\"Page confirms current Boltz-1/Chai-1/OpenFold3 support, but not the Apr 9, 2026 commit date, version 1.3.0, or the Cell Reports AAV-hCA4-IV77 publication.\"},{\"ref\":\"p2:c1\",\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"page_quote\":\"Consequently, when AlphaFold-Multimer was used, 10 independent models were generated for each competition because AlphaFold-Multimer gives five different predictions for each input, while ESMFold produced two different models for each competition.\",\"note\":\"Page also describes averaging scores and point-based round-robin ranking.\"},{\"ref\":\"p2:c2\",\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"page_quote\":\"The HT-APPRAISE screening took 24 h using three parallel Google Colaboratory GPU sessions and a laptop computer.\",\"note\":\"Adjacent text gives approximately 0.1–1 GPU minute per peptide-LY6A model and under 1 s per model on CPU, matching the item.\"},{\"ref\":\"p2:c3\",\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"page_quote\":\"Some false negatives were also observed, however, as in 9P08 with LY6A or 9P36 with CA-IV.\",\"note\":\"Page reports matrices for LY6A, LY6C1, and mouse CA-IV and documents the false negatives.\"},{\"ref\":\"p2:c4\",\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"page_quote\":\"Five structure models were produced using a protocol with up to 20 recycles, and MSA generated with MMseqs2 (UniRef+Environmental) and templates from PDB70.\",\"note\":\"Methods specify an A100 SXM4 40GB GPU, and the paper validates LRP6 binding in macaque and human primary brain microvascular endothelial cells plus cryo-ET.\"},{\"ref\":\"p2:done\",\"status\":\"PARTIAL\",\"page_quote\":\"Each model was recycled three times, and 10 models were generated from each competition.\",\"note\":\"The cited 2023 paper supports the ten-model matrices, PHP.eB–LY6A pose, and false negatives, but the five-model LRP6 modeling and cryo-ET work is from a different publication (the 2024 Nature Communications paper), not this page.\"},{\"ref\":\"p3:step\",\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"page_quote\":\"Dyno's novel generative AI models, trained on billions of in vivo measurements, most recently accelerated with NVIDIA hardware and software, using Hopper GPUs on DGX Cloud and libraries such as TransformerEngine, integrate sequence- and structure-based approaches to engineer functional capsids for new and promising BBB-crossing mechanisms with exceptional efficiency.\",\"note\":\"The release also describes multiple BBB mechanisms (TfR1, ALPL, Dyno-discovered receptors) and head-to-head in vivo comparison against a benchmark capsid.\"},{\"ref\":\"p3:activity\",\"status\":\"PARTIAL\",\"page_quote\":\"Launched in 2026, the Dyno-9zh is a top-performing capsid that achieves both exceptional brain transduction with significant liver detargeting in NHPs and mouse.\",\"note\":\"Page confirms 2026 launches of Dyno-9zh/yp2 and an ASGCT 2026 launch, but not the Jan 12, 2026 date or Roche/Novartis/Sarepta/Astellas partnerships.\"},{\"ref\":\"p3:c1\",\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"page_quote\":\"In parallel with its work on TfR1-mediated delivery, Dyno is advancing capsids that engage additional BBB transport pathways, including several BBB-receptors discovered by Dyno, as well as approaches involving alkaline phosphatase (ALPL), a compelling and distinct mechanism with translational relevance across species.\",\"note\":\"Directly supports the multi-mechanism portfolio and translatability rationale.\"},{\"ref\":\"p3:c2\",\"status\":\"PARTIAL\",\"page_quote\":\"Best capsid when compared head-to-head with other ALPL-targeting capsids in mouse and NHP.\",\"note\":\"Page supports head-to-head in vivo validation of ALPL-targeting capsids in mouse and NHP and describes ALPL engagement, but does not state the GPI-anchored receptor class.\"},{\"ref\":\"p3:c3\",\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"page_quote\":\"Dyno's Low-Shot Efficient Accelerated Performance (LEAP SM) technology, paired with the capability to make billions of in vivo sequence-function measurements each month, enables optimization of capsids for therapeutic success at an accelerated rate.\",\"note\":\"Release is dated October 24, 2024 and states Roche paid US$50 million upfront for a neurological-disease collaboration.\"},{\"ref\":\"p3:done\",\"status\":\"PARTIAL\",\"page_quote\":\"Engages human Alkaline Phosphatase (ALPL) receptor for BBB-crossing, supporting translation to humans.\",\"note\":\"Page supports ALPL engagement and head-to-head in vivo validation, but not the structure-based generative-design claim; the negative claim about exhaustive pose enumeration is not verifiable from this page.\"}]}","time":{"start":1792551870683,"end":1792551875630}}}
